I might try to write a Python script to merge the sections into one page 
(like the wavelessons).
It would probably be more rewarding than manually cutting and pasting.

I came up with a different idea, for a quick solution. Make a custom Google 
search. ;D
https://www.google.com/cse/publicurl?cx=005736688684443876844:0e9wzg2anpe
However, it fails to find things... try "ca ma"

I have been using Yahoo since before Google even existed anyhow,
so I decided to make myself a Yahoo custom search page (attached and only a 
single file)!
For those unfamiliar with limiting a search to one website, you would 
search for "ca ma" like this:
site:http://lojban.github.io/cll/ ca ma

Producing the first part of that is what will slow you down... so the html 
document I made takes care of that.
Simple javascript places the keyboard caret at the end successfully on 
Firefox, but IE blocks it... u'i

I also added a second input to show how easily someone can add more...
simply copy and paste, then change the 'id' and 'value' attributes of the 
input.

Press enter to search ;-] (opens in a new tab)

